{"title":"2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, a square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is partially shaded.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The largest shaded region is a square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The other two shaded regions are squares with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the total area of the unshaded region?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/099d0f0ad0adb7e1e6feb54bc013acd4ec3904f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 12 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 18 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 22 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 24 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the unshaded area, we can subtract the shaded area from the total area.\n</p><p>Since the total area is represented by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square\" title=\"Square\">square</a> with length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, its area is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242bade7eecb8dbe7d1ef62e8008cfb581dbe77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2 = 36$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We can find the area of each of the shaded squares as well, and add them together, giving us the total shaded area:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bb56d5e7cbea7b901a5c559c43b1cb77b4b0716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2 = 9$\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cb0e6e64d73bacef9c8869039bc21581f1884e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/312d643c239f9fd6054701a8cba664779329cf72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c627d6e982c05e83c96f63da528b49771d364e9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + 4 + 1 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the unshaded area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/c/d3c501fd9c163566acfeaa699e77b947ca6889fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 - 14 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 22}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"149\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?ti